<title>USA: U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS FELL IN LATEST WEEK.</title>
<headline>U.S. JOBLESS CLAIMS FELL IN LATEST WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Labor Department report of initial state jobless benefit claims, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p>Week Ended Initial Claims  4-Week Avg.  Continued Claims   - 07/26/97     277,000	325,750	Unavailable</p>
<p>  - 07/19/97     299,000	340,750	2,335,000</p>
<p>  - 07/12/97     341,000	349,000	2,333,000-R</p>
<p>  - 07/05/97     386,000	350,750	2,305,000-R</p>
<p>R-Revised, July 12 Continued Claims from 2,302,000 and July 5 from 2,300,000.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast initial jobless claims</p>
